{"id":"468172742","kind":"article","title":"间隔重复记忆系统让记忆更加自动化，从而有助于更深入的琢磨思考","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3hyucvGpCUB361PCegiHbX7FyFHcqZZF2pKK"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"间隔重复 & 注意力管理","date":"2022-02-16","updated":"2022-10-29","votes":16,"comment_count":0,"minutes":1,"chars":712,"keywords":["间隔重复","概念理解","记忆卡片","检索练习","助记媒介"],"summary":"译文认为，间隔重复能把基础事实的记忆自动化，使学习者把更多精力放在有意义的概念上；但它的用途不应限于死记硬背，也可以通过精心设计的问题促进概念性理解。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/468172742","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"参考文献"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"Pch5FGar\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zQiumA4k3SXo1GeRVJpsrVaBRETAoyYmSERS\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">深入理解需要详细的基础知识</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>。那么，看待<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4eXdSMJFv2qVGXSUEKH4vdcHBrLHcFY1ZGfC\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>的作用的一个角度是，它们有效地将学习中基础但需要死记硬背的知识自动化，以便你可以专注于更有趣、有意义或概念性的知识。</p><p data-pid=\"DeSIWnS4\">这是对<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zD5zaKmvTFAAL3PTJGWzkAQr6CtoBCdoXBpM\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">许多人认为记忆对深入的创造性工作不重要</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup>的很好的反驳。</p><p data-pid=\"MkxOBzTw\">不过，值得指出的是，间隔重复并不<b>只</b>对学习中最死板的部分有用：只是这种方式最容易使用。事实上，<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z6UZP7P4sRNgRKSvNj7tMV5uW6dDhwwbdZCy9\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">间隔重复记忆系统可以用来发展概念性理解</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup>。</p><hr/><p data-pid=\"s7fTU18a\">问：间隔重复如何帮助你把更多的精力用在深入的琢磨思考上？<br/>答：它可以自动化学习中的许多死记硬背的知识。</p><hr/><h2 id=\"sec-1\">参考文献</h2><p data-pid=\"ylQfez0P\">Matuschak, A., &amp; Nielsen, M. (2019, October 0). <i>How can we develop transformative tools for thought?</i> <sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup><a class=\"external\" href=\"https://numinous.productions/ttft\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"visible\">numinous.productions/tt</span><span class=\"invisible\">ft</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a> (see <a class=\"external\" href=\"https://numinous.productions/ttft/#how-important-is-memory\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"visible\">numinous.productions/tt</span><span class=\"invisible\">ft/#how-important-is-memory</span><span class=\"ellipsis\"></span></a>)</p><h2 id=\"sec-2\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"ukYn_-g-\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">间隔重复记忆系统</a></li><li data-pid=\"n-M2xbuj\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"454266265\" href=\"#/post/454266265\">许多人认为记忆对深刻的创造性工作不重要</a></li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-3\">声明</h2><p data-pid=\"EXe-X8pe\">此内容发布由 Andy Matuschak 许可。未经允许，不得转载或修改。保留所有权利。</p><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"RdT_bbyS\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z3hyucvGpCUB361PCegiHbX7FyFHcqZZF2pKK\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Spaced repetition memory systems help you focus on deeper engagement by automating away rote memorization (andymatuschak.org)</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 深刻的理解需要详细的基础知识 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"403208725\" href=\"#/post/403208725\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"404257681\" href=\"#/post/404257681\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 许多人认为记忆对深刻的创造性工作不重要 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"454266265\" href=\"#/post/454266265\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 间隔重复记忆系统可用于发展概念性理解 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"398045447\" href=\"#/post/398045447\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-5\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-5\">↩</a> 我们如何才能开发出变革性的思想工具？ <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"394795804\" href=\"#/post/394795804\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"466828742","title":"间隔重复记忆系统可以缩短科目学习中不愉快的早期阶段","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":19,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"470710559","title":"间隔重复系统中选择去记忆某项内容的行为有如轻松的手势","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":15,"minutes":2,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · 间隔重复 & 注意力管理"},{"id":"394795804","title":"我们如何才能开发出变革性的思想工具？","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":219,"minutes":89,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"403208725","title":"深刻的理解要求细致掌握基础知识","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":22,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"454266265","title":"许多人认为记忆对深刻的创造性工作不重要","author":"Andy Matuschak","votes":32,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"594372725","title":"用间隔重复软件记住一门编程语言","author":"Derek Sivers","votes":230,"minutes":8,"reason":"跨作者共鸣「记忆卡片」· Derek Sivers"}],"rec_answers":[]}